# Krab branding

Krabber's users, and anything branded, are **krabs** with a K. Anything a person
can read or type uses the K spelling:

| Write | Not |
|---|---|
| krab, krabs, Krab King, Baby Krab | crab, crabs, Crab King, Baby Crab |
| krabtag, `%tag` is a krabtag | crabtag |
| Krabmin (moderation) | Crabmin |
| `/krabs/<name>`, `/krab/login`, `/krabtag/<tag>`, `/krabmin` | `/crabs/...`, `/crab/...`, `/crabtag/...`, `/crabmin` |

This covers templates, flash and error messages, emails, placeholders, `aria-label`
and `title` text, JavaScript strings, robots.txt, and the real-animal jokes too
("We don't test on krabs").

What stays as it is:

- **Crabber**, the original project Krabber is ported from (docs, comparisons, credits).
- Code identifiers and internal names: `store.Crab`, `CrabID`, `crabs.go`, `crab-row`
  and other CSS classes and IDs, sprite IDs like `#crab`, template file names,
  DynamoDB keys and attributes, log and error-wrapping strings (`"create crab: %w"`).
- The old `/crabs`, `/crab/`, `/crabtag`, `/crabmin` URLs, which only exist as
  permanent redirects to the K versions (`legacyRedirects` in `internal/web/routes.go`).

```html
<!-- ❌ -->
<p>This crab hasn't filled out their bio</p>
<a href="/crabs/{{ .UserName }}">
<!-- ✅ -->
<p>This krab hasn't filled out their bio</p>
<a href="/krabs/{{ .UserName }}">
```

Before finishing a change that adds user-facing text, search the diff for
`[Cc]rab` (ignoring `Crabber` and identifiers) and fix any that a user would see.
